<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/TCM_TO#"
     xml:base="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/TCM_TO"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:ns4="http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/"
     xmlns:ns5="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/TCM_TO/"
     xmlns:ns6="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/TCM_TO">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="http://OntoTCM.org.cn/ontologies/TCM_TO/1.9.17"/>
        <dc:creator>OntoTCM working group</dc:creator>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">A bilingual OWL ontology of traditional Chinese medicine body structures integrated with modern anatomy, aligned with ICD-11, FMA and SNOMED CT. Release 1.8.1: unified namespace, removed subsumption cycles, migrated terminology mappings to annotation-based (skos:exactMatch) representation.</dc:description>
        <dc:title xml:lang="en">Traditional Chinese Medicine Body-structure Ontology (TCM-BO)</dc:title>
        <dc:title xml:lang="zh-cn">中医身体结构本体</dc:title>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">1.9.10 (2026-08-20): added normative bilingual definitions and provenance annotations for the four individual IRIs split in 1.9.9 (punning remediation); JFact full-classification run on 1.9.9 terminated at the 85-minute limit without reporting any inconsistency (historically inconsistency was detected within seconds); static type-conflict check 0; ELK consistent. 1.9.11 (2026-08-20): five mutual-correspondence pairs remodelled onto the new symmetric property has Symmetric Correspondence (TCM_HAO_00000000000000000831). 1.9.12 (2026-08-20): mapping adjudication applied - six cross-cultural false matches removed together with their identifier annotations and name restrictions. 1.9.13 (2026-08-24): label governance - all 21 same-language multi-label entities resolved (15 spurious mapping-residue English labels removed, 3 language-mis-tagged labels removed, 3 genuine English synonyms moved to has_exact_synonym); per-language multi-label count is now zero. 1.9.14 (2026-08-25): expert-adjudicated English label disambiguation - 187 duplicate-label assignments relabelled following three-expert majority vote (181 draft proposals adopted, 7 expert-modified labels applied); 20 class-merge candidates and 2 label-text adjudications deferred to PI decision. 1.9.15 (2026-08-25): PI-adjudicated structural consolidation - 17 duplicate class pairs merged with axiom and annotation migration (three-expert endorsed, PI confirmed), one TCM classical label applied (pomen), five Chinese label typos corrected; five merge pairs with conflicting ICD-11/FMA identifier annotations held for re-adjudication. 1.9.16 (2026-08-25): PI-adjudicated resolution of the five held merge pairs - broad ligament and rectosigmoid junction merged with target-side identifiers retained, labial commissure and orbit merged with source-side identifiers retained, and flexor pollicis brevis merged after correcting the target's misassigned ICD-11 annotation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">1.9.11 (2026-08-20): expert-review remodeling. Five mutual 635 (hasCorrespond) pairs with unclear directionality moved to a new symmetric property TCM_HAO_00000000000000000831 (has Symmetric Correspondence / 相应于), subPropertyOf 670 (has Func Cross Link), no domain/range; static check 0; ELK consistent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">1.9.12 (2026-08-20): adjudication of 58 discordant mapping pairs from the double-blind kappa review (kappa=0.612). Six spurious cross-cultural mappings removed together with their same-layer identifier annotations and target-name restrictions; two downgrade rulings were no-ops (already closeMatch). Static check 0; ELK consistent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">1.9.8 (2026-08-19): expert-reviewed restoration. Restored 42 property assertions deleted in 1.9.7 (12 hasXiangBiaoLi 661, 8 hasWesternCounterpart 688, 22 hasCorrespond 635); rerouted 7 assertions with western-medicine objects from 635 to 688; broadened ObjectPropertyDomain/Range of 634 (opens-at) from 3468/3407 to 3401 per expert review. Static type-conflict check: 0; ELK consistent.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">1.9.9 (2026-08-19): split class/individual punning for 4 IRIs (spleen TCM_HAO_0000068, pericardial cavity 0001345, cardia 0001674, perineum 0003400); individuals moved to TCM_HAO_90000000000000XXXX IRIs so that OWL1-style reasoners (JFact) no longer conflate them; ELK/JFact/static checks all clean.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">P0+P1 curation release derived from TCM_BO_1.8.0.owl on 2026-07-28; 1.9.0 adds Aristotelian bilingual definitions for 144 TCM-core classes (expert-review drafts); 1.9.1 restores OWL DL legality by converting 12 qualifiedCardinality restrictions on the non-simple transitive-related property has-part (TCM_TO_0000056) to someValuesFrom; 1.9.2 restores HermiT-reported consistency: removed 2 conflicting rdfs:domain axioms on datatype property has-anatomical-location, removed 4 spurious equivalentClass axioms on urine-production-and-excretion (incl. a false equivalence with immune response), and removed 2 over-asserted disjointness memberships (urine-excretion vs its parent kidney-qi-urine-role; ovary vs its parent uterine-adnexa); 1.9.3 fixes ABox-level and property-characteristic consistency: removed 9 reverse-direction assertions on asymmetric TCM relations (body-tissue correspondence, organ-orifice opening) and 2 self-loops, corrected the range of datatype property physio-index-reference from xsd:integer to xsd:string, and removed the erroneous SymmetricProperty declaration on has-Correspond (inverse of asymmetric opens-into). 1.9.4 systematic consistency release: shrunk machine-generated disjointness where it conflicted with the curated multiple-inheritance hierarchy (removed 333 ancestor-conflicting AllDisjointClasses memberships incl. the conflict-kernel of the organ-system and morphology blocks; removed hierarchy-conflicting disjointWith axioms; removed 7 mapping-era equivalentClass axioms bridging disjoint function classes; stripped self-contradictory domain/range axioms of the exterior-interior- 1.9.5 ABox consistency release: removed one wrongly-directed has-Correspond (635) assertion from each of 7 mutual-correspondence pairs that violated the asymmetry of kai-qiao-yu (634) via inverseOf reasoning (directions retained per TCM zang-fu/orifice theory; all logged to consistency_fixes_review.csv); retargeted the has-Western-Counterpart (688) assertion of Spleen(TCM) from the TCM-branch pancreas class to the western-branch pancreas individual (TCM_HAO_00000000000000000787), resolving the range clash between disjoint modern/TCM  1.9.6 ABox consistency release (continued): removed the FunctionalProperty characteristic from has-Western-Anat-Ref (685) and has-System-Affiliation (776); both are free-text narrative reference fields that legitimately carry multiple values, and the functional restriction caused 4 literal-distinctness inconsistencies (Stomach 578 and Gallbladder 3473 on 685; individuals 740 and 786 on 776).  1.9.7 reasoner-kernel consistency release: axiom-level ddmin (delta-debugging) isolated a 9-axiom minimal inconsistency kernel (InverseObjectProperties(634,635) + ObjectPropertyDomain(634,zang-fu 3468) + meridian subclass chain 09-08-03-02-01 + DisjointClasses(01, 3436, 3468) + one has-Correspond assertion forcing lung-meridian individual 686 into the disjoint zang-fu class). Removed all correspondence assertions that force individuals into mutually disjoint classes (meridian or western-branch individuals used as objects of has-Correspond/kai-qiao-yu), and removed the erroneous SameIndividual(642 anterior-yin, 643 posterior-yin) which merged two anatomically distinct orifices and created an asymmetry-violating 634 cycle through their bone/organ correspondences.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.9.17</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


